Entries for the Oklahoma QSO Party used by in-state (Oklahoma) stations
The 77 Oklahoma counties (each its own multiplier), the 50 states with DC counted as Maryland, and the 13 Canadian provinces and territories.
DXCC countries other than the USA, Canada, Hawaii and Alaska are the class's DX multiplier, not entries here.
The county file comes FIRST, so a county code wins over any state or province alias spelled the same.
DC is mapped to Md before S50.DOM (the rules: DC counts as Maryland).
NF and LB are read as NL (the last line), as nebraska.dom does; the rules list NL.
No line of this header may hold an equals sign: the reader takes any such line as an entry.
http://k5cm.com/okqp.htm

INCLUDE FILE oklahoma_cty.dom
Dc > Md = DC
INCLUDE FILE S50.DOM
INCLUDE FILE P13.DOM
Nl = NF,LB
